            <ArticleTitle>[Assessment of myocardial perfusion using digital subtraction angiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To assess myocardial perfusion, intra-aortic digital subtraction angiography (IADSA) was performed. Functional images are generated by taking a series of myocardial enhancement images. For each pixel, maximum density of enhancement (Cmax), integrated enhancement area under the curve (Cinteg), mean transit time (MTT) and Cmax/MTT or Cinteg/MTT were extracted. DSA was applicable for evaluating myocardial perfusion in patients with ischemic heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
